

--> Logging Basics & SLF4J
    Why Logging is Important in Enterprise Applications
    Logging helps you:
        Debug issues in production
        Track application flow
        Identify failures and performance issues
        Audit user activities
        Avoid using System.out.println() (not professional)
    👉 In real projects, logs = production visibility


--> What is SLF4J?
    SLF4J (Simple Logging Facade for Java) is:
        A facade (wrapper) for logging frameworks
        Works with Logback, Log4j2, JUL, etc.
    ✅ Advantage:
        You can change logging framework without changing code

--> Spring Boot & SLF4J Integration
    Spring Boot:
        Uses SLF4J + Logback by default
        No extra dependency needed
        Logger is auto-configured

